    reference 2-step; glider translated correctly.

BUGFIX #2 (upstream, MORKL.scala): `subs` and `collect` did NOT recurse into the Space/
Path argument of Grounded nodes (GroundedPP/SP/PS/SS) — they returned the node unchanged
(subs) or `???` (collect). So variable substitution by ANY Lower rule silently skipped
terms buried inside grounded functions. Fatal here: IterateLiteral_Union unrolled the GoL
iteration but left the bound Deref(x) inside card(...) = GroundedSP(neigh(x,y) ...), giving
a dangling ref at eval. Fixed both to recurse into the grounded argument (sound: it only
changes the value fed to the opaque function). (My Matching.subst/canon already recursed.)

Note: also found my Scala GoL *reference* under-counted (mutable map withDefaultValue+= ),
fixed; MORKL's encoding was correct all along (the existing `gol` test only checked a
4-cell sparse pattern, so dense correctness was previously unverified — now it is).

