## 2026-06-22 — final state: 93 passing / 0 failing / 4 ignored

Concrete artifact — SC of the semi-naive TC solver applied to the static graph {a.b,b.c,c.d}
yields a graph-specialized recursive loop (the static graph is fused in as a literal; the
accumulator #g0 and frontier #g1 are generalized to parameters):

  top: sn_tc_sc1()
  sn_tc_sc1() := Literal{a.b,b.c,c.d} \/ sn_tc_sc2(Literal{a.b,a.c,b.c,b.d,c.d}, Literal{a.c,b.d})
  sn_tc_sc2(#g0, #g1) := #g0 \/ sn_tc_sc2(
        #g0 \/ (#g1.iter(n, nbs, n x \/(Literal{a.b,b.c,c.d} <| nbs)) \ #g0),
              (#g1.iter(n, nbs, n x \/(Literal{a.b,b.c,c.d} <| nbs)) \ #g0))

This is the headline positive-supercompilation outcome: recursion specialized to static data
+ generalization of the dynamic accumulators into a compact, data-size-independent loop.

