## 2026-06-24 — pure (grounded-free) sliding puzzle + n-queens; evalT optimizations

Replaced the grounded Sliding/NQueens examples with PURE MORKL programs (no GroundedSS/PS):
- NQueens.Board(n): arithmetic precomputed into literal relations add/sub/upto; `aoe` routine =
  "attacks-or-equal"; place(k,n) nests `iterk`. A solution = distinct length-n prefix of the
  result paths (Trie.prefixCount). Generalizes to any n by rebuilding the tables.
- Sliding.Puzzle(rows,cols): cells c0..c(rc-1); `moves`/`all_moves` are swap-permutation
  relations; `superpose` labels a compact state, `collapse` re-compacts, `explore` is BFS to a
  fixpoint. Generalized from the bespoke 2x2 via an n-ary `iterN` helper (nests Iterations
  exposing each head as a named PathRef, since the DSL `iter` only goes to 4-tuples). Provides
  `expandStep` for bounded BFS and an independent Scala `refReachable` cross-check.
Verified counts: 2x2 = 12 (=4!/2); 3x3 = 181440 (=9!/2); n-queens 8=92, 9=352, 10=724,
11=2680, 12=14200 (OEIS A000170). NO grounded functions in either.

Two general evalT optimizations (sound; benefit all domains):
- short-circuit: when an operand is empty, skip evaluating the other for the annihilating ops
  (∩, ·, <|, \||, wrap, unwrap) — avoids the many empty guarded branches in the puzzle's
  union-of-cases formulation.
- literal-trie memo: cache Literal -> Trie by identity, so stable literal tables (n-queens
  add/sub/upto, accessed thousands of times) build their trie once.
These flipped pure n-queens from 0.5x (slower) to 12.7x faster on the trie.

Benchmarks (BENCHMARKS.md) — eval (Set) vs evalT (trie), with/without SC, ALL six domains now
pure algebra: datalog 24.6x, aunt 21.3x, temperature 58-882x, GoL 4.7x, sliding 3.2-4.0x,
n-queens (pure) 4.1x->12.7x, meet-all 18-116x. Geometric mean 9.0x overall / 10.3x across the
six example domains. SC residual on the trie matches/beats plain trie for datalog and n-queens.

Pure 3x3 full BFS = 181440 is correct but ~10 min (the price of no grounded functions); kept as
a Slow-tagged test. Suite (excluding Slow) **116 passing / 0 failing**. Slow tests cover full
3x3, 4x4/5x5 bounded BFS, and n-queens 9..12.

