## step: loop-invariant SUBGRAPH hoisting in push_out (extends item 10)  [DONE]
- push_out now hoists whole loop-invariant subgraphs, not just flat nodes.  A subgraph's earliest
  legal scope = deepest scope among its EXTERNAL dependencies = its source + every reference its
  WHOLE SUBTREE makes outside that subtree (so it lifts to just inside the innermost loop any part
  of it needs).  The scope tree is then re-derived from subgraph placements (a hoisted subgraph
  re-parents its child scope) and levels recomputed.  Sound because a scope's external refs subsume
  its subtree's, so a scope is never hoisted above an extract a descendant uses.  Result-subgraphs
  are pinned (their output must stay).  `hoistSubgraphs` flag (default true) enables clean A/B.
- Verified semantics-preserving by the 300-random-program property test + all existing tests
  (156/0) + a structural test (an invariant inner iteration lifts to root; both off/on == eval).
- A/B benchmark (SubgraphHoistBench, BENCHMARKS.md) — ONLY the hoist flag differs:
    invariant-inner N=150: 1.7x ; N=400: 3.4x (scales with outer-loop size; depth 2->1)
    sliding expandStep 3x3: 4.1x (the all_moves sub-iteration hoisted out of the explore loop)
    n-queens place(6): 1.1x (no loop-invariant inner loop — honest no-op)

