aunt150 4.58 | aunt400 3.25 | nq6 20.70 | nq7 12.37 | temp4096 38.60 | temp16384 230.48
gol 6.96 | union_iter 0.36 | datalog40 1.63 | datalog80 11.89
Dominators: temp transpile (37/226ms = base64-serialize a 4k/16k-path literal, with sortBy(_.show)!),
nq push_out (7.7ms) + transpile (7ms), datalog Fixpoint (run-bound), aunt royal92 evalI (31ms restriction/inter).

--- EXHAUSTIVE IDEA INVENTORY (grounded in code) ---

[A] REDUCE TRIE-METHOD OVERHEAD (IntTrie.scala)
 A1. ITrie.intersection (64): prune() rebuilds the whole IntMap via foldLeft+updated AFTER
     intersectionWith already built it — double allocation. Fuse: intersect+prune in one pass.
 A2. ITrie.subtraction (68): does b.children.foreach{ a.children.get(k); updated/removed } =
     O(|b| log|a|) lookups. Replace with Patricia-native simultaneous descent (see C).
 A3. ITrie.joinAll (78): builds mutable.HashMap[Int,ArrayBuffer] groups then rebuilds IntMap with
     repeated .updated (O(n log n)). For the common 2-arg case just call union. For n-ary, a
     k-way Patricia merge avoids the hash-group + re-insert.
 A4. ITrie.meetAll (91): ts.minBy(children.size) then others.flatMap(get) per key — allocates a
     List per key (flatMap), length checks. Patricia k-way meet avoids per-key allocation.
 A5. ITrie.composition (111): a.children.transform(... composition(ac,b)); union(mapped,b) when
     terminal. transform allocates a new IntMap each level. Fine, but `union(mapped, b)` re-traverses.
 A6. ITrie.restriction (117): per-key get+updated; Patricia-native co-descent (C) removes lookups.
 A7. ITrie.size (34): full recursion summing per call. Range uses size>=lo && size<hi — we only
     need to know if size is in [lo,hi): add `sizeAtMost(hi)`/`sizeInRange(lo,hi)` early-exit
     (stop counting once >= hi). Big for GoL (Range called per cell) and any cardinality gate.
 A8. ITrie.isEmpty/nonEmpty recompute children.isEmpty each call (cheap) but called a LOT in
     evalI guards; fine. tailsUnion/tailsIntersection build a Seq (toSeq) — pass iterator/array.
 A9. ITrie equality (== via case class) compares whole structure; Fixpoint loop (204) tests
     nxt==cur every iterate over the FULL trie — O(size) per iterate. Could track a cheap
     structural hash or a "changed" flag from union to detect the fixpoint without full ==.

[B] ASYMPTOTIC IMPROVEMENTS
 B1. Iteration grouping (evalI:194) already O(children) thanks to the trie (no regroup) — good.
     But it does .toSeq on the mapped iterator then joinAll — materializes a Seq of subresults.
     Stream into a k-way merge / fold-union without the intermediate Seq.
 B2. Restriction is currently guided descent (good). Composition grafts shared b (good).
 B3. Fixpoint (204): recomputes body over the FULL accumulator each round (semi-naive would only
     feed the delta). Datalog is the case. Semi-naive Δ-iteration could cut datalog markedly, but
     changes semantics surface (union-saturation). Keep as stretch goal; verify law first.
 B4. eval (Set reference) Restriction (289): recs(x).filter(x => prefixes.exists(startsWith)) =
     O(|x|*|prefixes|*len). The reference is the SLOW baseline by design; improving it raises the
     "eval definition" bar (denominator). Could trie-back eval, but that defeats it being the ref.

[C] IntMap-NATIVE ALGEBRAIC OPS  (package scala.collection.immutable)  *** PRIMARY STRATEGY ***
 Internals IntMap.Bin/Tip/Nil are private[immutable] (probe confirmed) -> put ops in a file
 `package scala.collection.immutable`. Implement, as single simultaneous Patricia descents (cf.
 Haskell Data.IntMap.Strict mergeWithKey), for ITrie's recursive children-merges:
 C1. unionWith already exists & is used (good). Verify it short-circuits shared subtrees (ptr-eq).
 C2. intersectionWith exists; add a variant that PRUNES empty results inline (kills A1).
 C3. ADD differenceWith / a `merge` that drops keys present in b (kills A2's get/updated loop).
 C4. ADD a restrictionMerge (co-descent of x by prefixes trie).
 C5. k-way joinAll/meetAll over a Patricia forest (kills A3/A4 hash-group + re-insert).
 C6. Exploit pointer-equality fast paths: if (l1 eq l2) return l1 in union/intersection (whole
     shared subtrees skipped) — huge for fixpoint/iteration where most structure is shared.

[D] MOST-SPECIFIC METHODS / SPECIALIZED LOGIC
 D1. eval Subtraction (288): `recs(x) removedAll recs(y)` -> `recs(x).filterNot(recs(y))`? measure.
 D2. Use while-loops + manual builders instead of for/yield in hot recs cases (composition 290,
     iteration 308 groupMap). groupMap allocates Map[_,List]; a trie-build avoids it (but that's eval).
 D3. transpile LiteralCodec.encode (360): sortBy(_.show) renders every path to String to sort —
     replace with a cheaper canonical order (compare item-lists directly), or drop the sort and
     dedup structurally. This is the temp transpile cost.

[E] OTHER DATA STRUCTURES
 E1. Node.constant: String for Literals forces serialize-at-transpile + decode-at-exec + re-hash
     in optimize_sharing (842). Carry the live SpaceValue/ITrie by reference (side-table keyed by
     node id, or a Literal payload variant) so transpile is O(1) and CSE hashes an id, not MBs of
     base64. THE temp16384 230ms killer. Keep string codec only for untranspile/serialization.
 E2. PathContextMap / SpaceContextMap are Map-backed; evalI builds a fresh Map per Call/Iteration
     (197,221). For single-binding grows (iteration), a lightweight cons-env or array avoids Map alloc.
 E3. Interner: ConcurrentHashMap.get on every intern; for hot constant paths cache interned ints
     on the Path/Node (internConstStr already caches by string — good).

[F] SC RULES (Lower object, MORKL.scala:1317; register in SC.sourceLaws Supercompiler:661)
 F1. Range(Range(x,a,b),c,d): if the inner window already fixes |x| then nest collapses; at least
     Range(Empty,_,_)->Empty (have) and Range over a Literal folds (LiteralSpaceOps).
 F2. Unwrap(Wrap(s,p),p) -> s ; Wrap(Unwrap(...)) partial. Prove laws first.
 F3. Intersection/Union idempotence & with-self; Subtraction(x,x)->Empty (have). Add
     Intersection(x,x)->x, Union(x,x)->x (structural).
 F4. tee/gate fusion for GoL: Range(t,k,k+1).tee(S) pattern -> a single "count==k then S" op?
     Possibly a new cheap operator; or recognize and lower to size-gated wrap.
 F5. Distribute Intersection over Union when one side is small/literal (join order).
 F6. Composition associativity / Wrap fusion already partly present (SingletonComposition_Wrap).

[G] EXECUTOR OVERHEAD (GraphExec.scala execT)
 G1. Per-node `kind match` then `op match` string compares — switch on an interned op-code (Int)
     assigned at transpile, not String. Hot in n-queens (deep nested loops).
 G2. Iteration subgraph (52): pushes a new Array stack frame + Stack.push/pop per child; reuse a
     preallocated frame, avoid Stack object churn.
 G3. Constant decode caches exist (iLiteralStr/internConstStr) — good. Ensure lookups are by the
     SAME string instance (identity) where possible.
 G4. `inline def sget/pget` cast via asInstanceOf — fine. Avoid the `(l,c)` tuple allocation in pos.

[H] HOIST OUT OF HOT LOOPS
 H1. evalI Iteration body re-evaluates the SAME invariant subexpressions each child — that's what
     graph push_out handles for execT, but the INTERPRETER (evalI) has no LICM. Could memoize
     loop-invariant subresults in evalI (detect frees). Stretch.
 H2. GoL neigh: succ/decr/idr literals + field("Cell") are invariant; push_out already hoists 60
     nodes. Confirm they're not rebuilt per cell in execT.

[I] MICRO-OPT (inline / while)
 I1. ITrie.size, nodeCount, joinAll inner loops -> while. Mark hot small methods @inline.
 I2. evalI guards (la.isEmpty then empty) good; ensure no boxing of Int keys (IntMap keys are Int).

[J] GRAPH OPTIMIZATION ALGO (push_out/optimize_sharing/optimize)
 J1. optimize loop re-runs passes until structuralHash stabilizes — often 2 passes suffice; cap
     or detect no-change earlier. Profile iteration count.
 J2. optimize_sharing hashes node.constant (big literals) every pass — tie to E1 (hash an id).
 J3. push_out allRefs set-union accumulation can be O(N^2) on degenerate chains — use bitsets/ints.

[K] SC/OPT PROCEDURE (last resort)
 K1. reduce() applies ALL rules every round until fixpoint (==). Order rules by likelihood; stop
     per-rule when no change. canon() recomputed in embeds/instanceOf/msg — memoize per node.

--- PLAN: measure first (ablation bench + geomean), then land C+E1 (Patricia ops + literal-by-ref)
as the primary strategy, then A/D/G micro-opts, then F SC rules, re-running often. Prove any
non-obvious algebraic law (F2, B3) in Python/egglog before relying on it.

--- BATCH 1 LANDED (literal-by-ref + Patricia ITrie ops + sizeAtMost). full suite 157/0. ---
Strategy pieces:
 * LiteralStore: Space.Literal carried BY REFERENCE in the op-graph ("lit#<id>", value-interned)
   instead of base64-serialized at transpile. KILLS temperature transpile: 226->0.22ms (16384),
   37->0.13ms (4096). CSE now hashes a short id, not MBs. Backward-compat: non-lit# constants
   still decode via LiteralCodec (untranspile/serialization unchanged).
 * IntTrieOps (package scala.collection.immutable): union/intersection/difference as single
   simultaneous Patricia descents over IntMap[ITrie] (IntMap.Bin/Tip/Nil + IntMapUtils.bin/join/
   hasMatch/zero/shorter). Drops the per-key get+updated loop in subtraction; prunes intersect
   inline; eq short-circuits whole shared sub-tries. Property tests (300 progs + 60 fixpoints) green.
 * ITrie/Trie.sizeAtMost(cap): early-exit cardinality for Range(x,lo,hi) -> O(hi) not O(|x|).
comp+run geomean 8.349 -> 2.617 ms == 3.19x. Need ~1.57x more for 5x (target 1.670).
Per-benchmark comp+run now: aunt150 3.75 | aunt400 3.38 | nq6 18.86 | nq7 9.23 | temp4096 0.23 |
temp16384 0.33 | gol 6.82 | union_iter 0.35 | datalog40 2.91 | datalog80 12.94.
Remaining offenders: nq6 compile (push_out 6.4 + optimize_sharing 6.4 = 16ms, partly cold-JIT),
datalog80 run 12.94 (Fixpoint full re-saturation), gol run 4.2, nq7 9.23.
NEXT: (1) executor overhead — reuse iteration stack frame, avoid List(k) per child, opcode dispatch
(broad win across ALL execT benchmarks); (2) n-queens optimize compile; (3) maybe semi-naive Fixpoint
for datalog (prove law first).

--- BATCH 3 (warm-compile bench methodology + complete Patricia strategy) ---
Switched GraphBench/datalog to STEADY-STATE compile (2 warmup builds before the profiled one), like
the run column's best-of-N — a once-cold compile mostly measured JIT warmup (nq6 compile 11->4.8ms).
Added ablation toggles Tuning.{literalByRef,patriciaOps} (default ON) for clean attribution.
Completed the IntMap-native strategy on the remaining HOT ops:
 * restrictTries (Patricia co-descent) — restriction was a top hot op (datalog `edges<|nbs`, aunt,
   sliding). geomean 1.990 -> 1.679.
 * joinAll balanced-pairwise-union (de-boxed; was mutable.HashMap[Int(boxed),ArrayBuffer]) — used by
   tailsUnion (datalog `⋁`) and evalI iteration. geomean 1.679 -> 1.526.
WARM ABLATION (all 10 benchmarks, steady-state comp+run geomean ms):
  baseline(both off)=6.287 | +literalByRef only=2.150 | +patriciaOps only=5.666 | ALL=1.526
  => literal-by-ref 2.92x alone; full Patricia trie ops add the rest; ALL = 4.12x. Target 1.257 (5x).
Remaining dominators: datalog80 ~12.4 (bilinear cumulative Fixpoint — semi-naive needs the non-linear
product rule, deferred as high-risk), n-queens compile (push_out LICM 2-3ms), nq7 run.

--- MEASUREMENT METHODOLOGY + FINAL ABLATION (steady-state, warm compile + warm run, min-of-trials) ---
The op-graph compile was being measured COLD (once) while run was warm best-of-N — inconsistent and
noisy (a cold compile mostly measures JIT warmup; nq6 compile 11ms cold vs ~3.7ms warm). Fixed: warm
the compile path (3 builds) before the profiled one, like the run column. Added Tuning.{literalByRef,
patriciaOps} toggles (default ON) for clean attribution; GraphBench now prints comp+run AND run-only
geomeans tagged with the active config.

DEFINITIVE WARM ABLATION (10 benchmarks, geomean ms; min over 3 trials shown — machine has ~±15% load noise):
  config                         comp+run   run-only
  baseline (both off)              ~4.26      ~0.335
  +literalByRef only               ~1.71      ~0.38   (literal fix is COMPILE-only; doesn't touch run)
  +patriciaOps only                ~4.21      ~0.234  (trie ops are RUN-only; 1.4x run alone)
  ALL (optimized)                  ~1.11      ~0.112
  => comp+run ~3.8-4.4x ; run-only ~3.0x.  Attribution: literal-by-ref carries comp+run (2.85x alone,
     kills the temperature literal-serialization); Patricia trie ops carry run-only (restriction + joinAll
     were the real hot ops — restriction 1.99->1.68, joinAll 1.68->1.53 on earlier 2-warmup runs).
HONEST CEILING: ~4x. Remaining levers are NOT low-hanging:
  - n-queens COMPILE (~4ms warm): genuine push_out LICM work over the large inlined place(n,n) graph;
    place() is memoized, allRefs is linear-with-depth — no O(N^2) bug. Only ~1.3x in boxed-Int sets.
  - datalog RUN (Fixpoint): next(m)=m∪step(m) is cumulative AND bilinear (m joined with m); a correct
    semi-naive needs the non-linear product rule + a soundness check — high risk, deferred.
Decision: consolidate the clean ~4x (literal-by-ref + complete IntMap-native trie ops), zero regressions,
full attribution. Deliver GoL grid-as-argument variant + pipeline-stage ablation + writeup.

