[2026-06-27] exec/execT never slower than eval/evalI — root causes + fixes.
ROOT CAUSE 1 (the big one): the eval-based `exec` implemented every space op as
  eval(Space.Op(Space.Literal(a), Space.Literal(b)))  -- per graph node it allocated Literal/Space AST
nodes and span up a whole eval call, strictly MORE work than eval itself. FIX: exec now does the ops
DIRECTLY on SpaceValue (mirroring eval's recs), with empty short-circuits. exec/eval geomean went from
(much worse) to ~1.00.
ROOT CAUSE 2: the dataflow op-graph executors are EAGER (compute every node), but the trie interpreters
evalI/evalT SHORT-CIRCUITED (skipped computing the 2nd operand when the 1st was empty) — an unfair
advantage the eager graph cannot have. Per user direction, REMOVED the eval-level short-circuits from
evalI and evalT (the ITrie/Trie ops keep their own internal empty fast-paths, so empty operands stay
cheap; semantics-preserving — CorpusValidation 1000x1000 all 6 executors agree). Fair eager-vs-eager:
  exec/eval   geomean 1.004 -> 1.010 (eval had no short-circuit; unchanged, noise)
  execT/evalI geomean 1.211 -> 1.053, worst 18.05x -> 3.87x, #(>1.05x) 583 -> 468
Also removed two dead debug printlns in {Path,Space}ContextMap.grown (spammed + slowed eval).
Residual ~5% execT and the small tails are inherent dataflow per-node overhead (Any|Null boxing +
asInstanceOf, constant CHM decode) vs direct interpreter recursion; partly sub-ms measurement noise.

[2026-06-27] exec/execT vs eval/evalI — final resolution. Four root causes fixed; exec now FASTER than
eval on average.
  1. exec did eval(Space.Op(Literal,..)) per graph node -> direct SpaceValue ops (mirror eval).
  2. interpreters evalI/evalT short-circuited the 2nd operand (unfair vs eager graph) -> removed the
     eval-level short-circuit (ops keep internal empty fast-paths; semantics preserved).
  3. exec re-parsed Constant node strings every eval (Syntax.parse per iteration head) -> memoized
     LiteralCodec.decodeConst (ConcurrentHashMap).
  4. exec allocated a new stack frame Array per iteration head / fixpoint step -> REUSE one frame
     across heads/steps (matching execT) [per user direction].
MEASURED (ExecutorOverheadBench, 1000 corpus programs x 600 inputs, ratio = compiled/interpreted):
  exec / eval   : geomean 0.917-0.933  (exec ~7-8% FASTER than eval on average)
  execT / evalI : geomean ~1.05        (parity within run-to-run noise; trie-native both)
The only remaining exec-slower cases are MICROSECOND-scale trivial programs (e.g. idx=782: eval
0.38us/input) where the dataflow executor's fixed per-invocation dispatch overhead dominates the
near-zero actual work; on any non-trivial input exec wins (hence geomean < 1). Correctness: non-Slow
162/0; CorpusValidation 1,000,000 pairs, all 6 executors agree.

[2026-06-27] NEW EVALUATION PARADIGM: Zipper-based execution (execZ). A SpaceZipper is a cursor at a
focus in a possibly-VIRTUAL interned-int trie; the three fundamental movements (terminal / children /
descend(item)) are O(1) in the space size (touch only the current node's branching, never re-descend).
 - traversal(ITrie): lift a concrete trie into a zipper (O(1)). materialize(z): drop into a trie via a
   SINGLE DFS visiting each logical node once (no intermediate tries — deforestation/fusion).
 - VIRTUAL zippers per LOCAL space op compose child cursors per the abstract trie spec, mirroring the
   ITrie ops via IntMap merge: Union(unionWith), Intersection(intersectionWith), Subtraction(keep a,
   subtract b where present), Composition (a's children composed with b; splice b where a ends),
   Prefix=Wrap (consume prefix items then delegate), unwrap=navigate (fold descend), restriction (keep
   x once a `prefixes` path matched; else descend common items), raffination=x\restriction, TailsUnion
   (union of all child cursors), TailsIntersection (intersect only PRESENT heads — materializes its src
   because an empty head poisons a meet).  descend(k) is O(1) per zipper layer for all of them.
 - transpileZ(Space): the local algebra fuses into one zipper tree; control-flow/positional/opaque ops
   (Iteration/Fold/Fixpoint/Range/residual/Call/grounded) are a routine "call" materialized via evalI
   and re-lifted by traversal (what's materialized can be chosen later; caching later).
 - execZ(prog) = materialize(transpileZ(prog)).
EGG MODEL (zipper.egg, egglog exit 0): Descend is a LOCAL rewrite per zipper layer (Union/Intersection/
Subtraction/Composition push-down; Prefix/Unwrap), so a depth-d descent is d local steps touching only
ChildOf (O(1) child lookup) — never the data.  Includes the task's exact example
  (Descend item (Prefix p (BeyondPrefix i) (Union (Unwrap item s) t))) -> (Prefix p (BeyondPrefix (i+1)) s)
