[2026-06-28] Reworked the egg coincidence to be PURELY BY DESCENT (no materialization).
Critique: the prior `(check (= $prog $want))` proved coincidence by materializing both sides — against
the whole point of zippers; and the fundamental examples were pre-materialized to Lit.
Now ZipperEgg.coincidenceProgram emits NO result-trie equality. Instead, the zipper's defining property:
  - every result member: descend to it -> focus Term = T  (you CAN descend to it);
  - every BOUNDARY non-member: descend to it -> Term = F   (you CANNOT) — boundary = at each reachable
    node, every program-vocabulary key (keysOf(z) ∪ result keys) that is NOT a child there.
