================================================================================
2026-07-12  AlgebraicResult for the TreeMap Trie ops (PathMap ring.rs analogue)
================================================================================
Plan: introduce a set-only AlgebraicResult (Empty | Identity(mask) | Bespoke(t))
for the pairwise Trie ops — union, intersection, subtraction, restriction,
raffination, composition — computed at EVERY trie node, so each op can return an
argument unchanged (structural sharing, zero allocation), collapse to empty
(annihilation, prunes the parent), or build a fresh node only when the result
genuinely mixes both sides.  Because spaces are pure sets of paths, stronger
laws hold than in pathmap's value-carrying AlgebraicResult<V>:
  union         Ident(L) <=> b <= a; Ident(R) <=> a <= b; Empty <=> both empty
  intersection  Ident    <=> that arg contained in the other (the smaller one);
                Empty <=> disjoint (incl. empty arg)
  subtraction   Ident(L) <=> a and b disjoint (b empty is the special case);
                result == right is NOT a case: a\b == b forces a == b == {} =
                Empty (ring.rs non-commutative rule: never set the counter bit)
  restriction   Ident(L) <=> every left path extends a right prefix;
                Ident(R) <=> result equals right as a set; Empty <=> either side
                empty or nothing prefixed
  raffination   fused single traversal (was subtraction(x, restriction(x, y)));
                Ident(L) <=> nothing prefixed; Empty <=> everything prefixed
                (right containing eps annihilates)
  composition   Ident(L) <=> right == {eps}; Ident(R) <=> left == {eps};
                Empty <=> either side empty (exact: a finite nonempty set is
                never closed under appending a non-eps path)
Old ad-hoc isEmpty short-circuits inside the ops are superseded by the case
analysis.  evalT behavior must be unchanged (TrieTest pins ops against eval);
TrieBench must not regress.
