  "cux" x (Head(s("foo")) u Head(s("bar"))).
Findings:
 1. The target form is NOT equivalent in general: with exactly one source empty
    the product is {} (a loop runs zero times) while the target still emits the
    other side.  The chain's "push out"/"push out loop" steps carry an implicit
    "both sources nonempty" precondition.  Asserted by eval in the suite.
 2. Literal (provably headed) sources: Routine.optimized overshoots the target
    -- IterUnion_Indep (the guarded push-out), IterateLiteral_Union (known
    unroll), ConcatSingleton_Iter/Wrap_Iter (destination specialization) and
    Literal_ConstantsUnion collapse the whole product to the literal result
    Literal({cux.a1, cux.a2, cux.b1, cux.b2}).
 3. Symbolic sources, Space level: Lower correctly REFUSES the hoist
    (IterUnion_Indep is guarded by provablyHeaded, which is false for a
    mention) -- semantics preserved on nonempty/one-sided/empty bindings.
 4. Symbolic sources, op-graph level: optimize = push_out + optimize_sharing
    achieves the sound part of the chain at runtime: loop-resident nodes
    15 -> 11 -- Unwrap(s, bar) hoisted out of the x-loop, Constant cux shared
    and hoisted to the top, Concat(cux, x)/Singleton(cux.x) hoisted from the
    y-body to the x-body (once per x instead of once per (x,y)).  The union
    accumulation stays inside the y-loop, so {}-sources stay {}: exec agrees
    with eval on all four bindings (both execT and exec).
NOT currently achieved for symbolic sources: hoisting the whole y-loop out of
the x-loop (the union node inside the y-body depends on x, and the graph has no
drain-chain reassociation to split it), the iter-add -> Head fusion (Head is
not a primitive; Syntax.head is itself an iter), and the final factoring
Wrap(a,p) u Wrap(b,p) -> Wrap(a u b, p).  All three would need either the
provably-headed guard or a runtime emptiness test to stay sound.

================================================================================
2026-07-13  Guarded product-into-union: emptiness factors + factoring rules
================================================================================
Goal: support the independent-product-to-union example end-to-end on SYMBOLIC
sources.  The soundness gap is closed by a constant-time emptiness factor:
  nonEmpty(x) = (x /\ {eps}) \/ Range(x,0,1).iter(_, _, {eps})   [user's def]
  headed(x)   = Range(x,-1,0).iter(_, _, {eps})
The ITERATION hoist needs headed(x), not nonEmpty(x): a source that is exactly
{eps} runs zero iterations (eps has no head), and nonEmpty({eps}) = {eps} would
leak the hoisted branch.  eps sorts FIRST in the canonical path order, so the
LAST path (Range(x,-1,0)) is headed iff any path is — still O(one path).
Planned:
 A. Lower: headedGuard/nonEmptyGuard combinators; IterUnion_Indep upgraded with
    a guarded fallback for non-provably-headed sources; IterComposition_Indep
    (hoisting an independent composition factor out of an iteration is sound
    UNguarded: composition distributes over the union of iterates, 0 iterates
    -> {} on both sides); EpsGuard_Wrap commute (Comp(g, Wrap(s,p)) ->
    Wrap(Comp(g,s), p) when g provably (= {eps}-subset); UnionWrap_Factor
    common prefix factoring (Wrap(a,p) u Wrap(b,p) -> Wrap(a u b, p)).
 B. push_out upgrade: split a loop whose RESULT is Union(a,b) with one operand
    hoisted out of the loop — synthesize the headed-guard subgraph at graph
    level (the drain-chain step); one split per pass, optimize()'s fixpoint
    loop iterates.  optimize_sharing already dedupes structurally equal guard
    subgraphs via its SG value-numbering.
--- checkpoint 1: both layers reach the target -----------------------------------
Space level (Routine.optimized): the symbolic product now optimizes to
  "cux" x (headed(s(bar)) x Head(s(foo))  \/  headed(s(foo)) x Head(s(bar)))
via guarded IterUnion_Indep -> IterComposition_Indep -> ConcatSingleton_Iter ->
EpsGuard_Wrap -> UnionWrap_Factor.  Literal sources still constant-fold fully.
Graph level (optimize): push_out gained the union split (synthesizes the
headed-guard subgraph: Range(src,-1,0).iter(_,_,{eps})) and the composition
split (no guard needed: {} annihilates composition).  Loop DEPTH 2 -> 1 on the
example: the y-loop hoists to the top, per-(x,y) work is gone, the eps constant
is shared between both guard bodies by optimize_sharing.
morkl.ProductUnionCheck: 6/6 green, incl. eps-only-source bindings (s("foo") =
{eps}) that pin why the guard must be HEADED, not nonEmpty.
Full battery (36 suites): green.  CorpusValidation + ExecutorOverheadBench
running.
--- checkpoint 2: sharing upgrade + validation ----------------------------------
optimize_sharing is now ALPHA-INVARIANT: Extract slots value-numbered by
position (not binder name), Iteration/Fixpoint root names dropped from subgraph
keys, plus an idempotence peephole collapsing interior pass-through Union(x,x)
nodes (the splits leave those).  Same-source product now collapses to the
ideal graph: ONE guard + ONE merged head-loop + one composition
(morkl.ProductUnionCheck "same-source product", 7/7 green).
Full battery re-run after each upgrade: 36 suites green.
CorpusValidation: 1,000,000 pairs, 7 executors agree (unchanged).
ExecutorOverheadBench (compiled/interpreted geomean, <1 faster):
  pre-change   execT/evalI 1.111  worst 8.90x
  after splits execT/evalI 1.091  worst 5.39x
  after alpha  execT/evalI 1.084  worst 5.56x   -- the upgrades net-help the corpus
SUPERCOMPILER.md optimizer section documents the splits, the headed guard, and
alpha-invariant sharing.  EquivPipelineTest (egg/z3/vampire) running.

